Subject: text-shimmer-v2: the band moves by transform on the compositor

What: the swept copy paints its muted text through background-clip: text and holds a
sweep, 3.6 times the text's width, whose mask is the band gradient. The sweep and the
peak copy inside it animate transform in opposite directions, so the glyphs stay put
while the band crosses them. The swept copy clips to its own box.
Why: a background-position sweep is not compositable and repainted every running
shimmer on the main thread each frame (240 paints/s for three tool rows).

